{"availability":"available","full":"thefinnomenon/oxe","name":"oxe","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2024-04-24T13:00:21Z","updated":"2026-10-08T02:29:49Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://oxe-playground.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://oxe-playground.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:37:40.202Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T15:37:40.202Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T15:37:40.202Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T15:37:40.202Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["OXE is an AI-first application language and runtime. Its long-term design is one compiler-visible graph spanning UI, asynchronous work, data, authorization, caching, errors, logs, metrics, and traces.","The project is being rebuilt from the UI language outward. Its production path does not use React, Solid, a virtual DOM, or innerHTML.","The compiler and runtime start in strict TypeScript. The web runtime must execute as JavaScript and call the DOM directly while the language and graph are changing quickly. Intermediate representations remain plain and serializable. The server render plan contains no JavaScript closures or DOM values, so a future Rust SSR backend can consume the same contract; measured compiler or rendering profiles can justify that move without changing authored language semantics."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/thefinnomenon/oxe/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f921e970459b06a89177ea7fa81ee41e96928ce9c699d15e31dfe650387fcdd1","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T15:37:40.390Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:37:40.390Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"OXE is an AI-first application language and runtime. Its long-term design is one compiler-visible graph spanning UI, asynchronous work, data, authorization, caching, errors, logs, metrics, and traces.","sour